The most addresses of this network the objects of this namespace may hold,
cluster-wide.

An allocation taking the namespace over it is refused, so one namespace cannot
drain a network the others are meant to share. Leave it unset for a namespace
that is not capped on this network.

Addresses are counted, not reservations: a failover object holds the same
address on every node it is configured on, and that is one address taken from
the network, while the instances of a flex each hold one of their own.

The limit is checked when an address is allocated, not when one already held
is asked for again, so a namespace that reached its limit still restarts what
it already runs.
